tize simplicity and learning over showing more information.\r\n\r\nOne important change: Don't show all 50 steps, all variables, a flowchart, and seven explanation cards simultaneously. Show just the current operation, a simple explanation, the changed variables, and a Next Step button. That will make learning much easier.\r\n\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-10T16:21:55+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
{"step_index":74,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-10T10:51:56Z","input_tokens":6090,"cache_read_tokens":192125,"output_tokens":8754,"thinking":"Carefully reviewing the request, the primary goal is a UI overhaul to create an accessible \"Teach Me This Code\" experience, maintaining the existing execution engine without AI integration. This suggests a focus on pedagogical design and user-centered interface elements rather than functional code changes. The core functionality within `engine.py` and `engine.js` should remain untouched.\n\n\nInitial focus is on interface transformation, preserving existing execution components. Modification will involve restructuring layout to a three-pane design: code display, step-by-step explanations, and variable value tracking. The UI should be simplified significantly with a light theme and increased readability. I will start by examining the existing UI components and identify the elements to be removed or modified.\n\n\nFocusing on the UI overhaul, the code editor will highlight the current line, dimming the rest to guide the user's attention. A subtle edit button will allow code or input list modification without cluttering the display. The teaching area will present steps sequentially, with code snippets and breakdowns of the calculations.\n\n\nThis code finds the largest sum you can get from a continuous section of the list. The explanation will begin with a simple overview. The function's definition will be shown, followed by its call. The program execution will iterate step-by-step, explaining each operation.\n\nNow it's at a negative value that will set the variable to zero. Next, Python moves to the next line and creates the variable `ans`. The largest continuous subarray `[4, -1, 2, 1]` results in a sum of 6.\n\n```\nFinal answer: 6\n```\nThe continuous section `[4, -1, 2, 1]` has the largest sum: 6.\n\n\nThe current section being considered, `[-5, -2, -8]`, yields a final answer of -2. The largest continuous sum identified is also -2, derived from the continuous section `[-2]`. The variable inspector displays the current values of `c` (0) and `ans` (-2). Navigation controls include `Previous`, a prominent `Next Step` button, `Auto Play`, and `Restart`.\n\n\nThe \"Advanced View\" feature's implementation requires modifying multiple files. This involves adding a toggle element and associated event listeners. The view itself will need to dynamically show/hide detailed debugging information within a collapsible section. The initial plan is to determine the optimal place for the toggle. It should also be styled unobtrusively.\n\n\nFocus shifts to augmenting the explainer for the \"Teach Me This Code\" view, aiming to provide a pedagogical breakdown of each execution step. Each step will include a `teacherLesson` object with a `stepTitle`, offering a concise, human-friendly title. This structure enables a more intuitive step-by-step learning experience.\n\n\nThe explainer will provide structured information for each step, including current number, before/after calculation values, and a conversational explanation of the code. It will also track relevant variable values and describe the next step's action. A final banner will highlight the largest subarray and its sum upon completion. This detailed breakdown aims to enhance the \"Teach Me This Code\" experience.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"// explainer.js — \"Teach Me This Code\" Rule-Based Teacher & Advanced Explanation Engine\n// Preserves full compatibility with engine.js while providing beginner-friendly teacher lessons.\n\nconst PYTHON_SYMBOLS_LIBRARY = [\n  { token: \"class\", label: \"class\", desc: \"Groups related functions together under one name.\" },\n  { token: \"def\", label: \"def\", desc: \"Creates a function (a reusable set of instructions).\" },\n  { token: \"for\", label: \"for\", desc: \"Repeats the indented lines once for each item in a list or range.\" },\n  { token: \"while\", label: \"while\", desc: \"Keeps repeating the indented lines as long as a condition is True.\" },\n  { token: \"range(\", label: \"range(len(nums))\", desc: \"Creates index numbers 0, 1, 2... up to the last position in the list.\" },\n  { token: \"+=\", label: \"+=\", desc: \"Adds a number to the existing variable and saves the new total.\" },\n  { token: \"-=\", label: \"-=\", desc: \"Subtracts a number from the existing variable.\" },\n  { token: \">=\", label: \">=\", desc: \"Asks: 'Is the left number greater than or equal to the right number?'\" },\n  { token: \"<=\", label: \"<=\", desc: \"Asks: 'Is the left number less than or equal to the right number?'\" },\n  { token: \"==\", label: \"==\", desc: \"Asks: 'Are these two values equal?'\" },\n  { token: \"<\", label: \"<\", desc: \"Asks: 'Is the left number smaller than the right number?'\" },\n  { token: \">\", label: \">\", desc: \"Asks: 'Is the left number larger than the right number?'\" },\n  { token: \"=\", label: \"=\", desc: \"Stores the value on the right inside the variable name on the left.\" },\n  { token: \"[\", label: \"nums[i]\", desc: \"Looks up the number at position `i` in the list `nums`.\" },\n  { token: \"return\", label: \"return\", desc: \"Finishes the function and gives back the final answer.\" }\n];\n\nclass RuleBasedExplainer {\n  enrichTraceWithExplanations(traceResult) {\n    if (!traceResult || !traceResult.steps) return traceResult;\n    const steps = traceResult.steps;\n\n    // Find the best contiguous subarray if `nums` is present so we can show it at the end\n    const bestSubarrayInfo = this.computeBestSubarray(traceResult);\n\n    for (let i = 0; i < steps.length; i++) {\n      const step = steps[i];\n      const prevStep = i > 0 ? steps[i - 1] : null;\n      const nextStep = i + 1 < steps.length ? steps[i + 1] : null;\n\n      step.teacherLesson = this.buildTeacherLesson(step, prevStep, nextStep, bestSubarrayInfo);\n      step.explanations = this.buildStepExplanation(step, prevStep, nextStep);\n      step.practiceQuestion = this.buildPracticeChallenge(step, nextStep);\n    }\n\n    traceResult.bestSubarrayInfo = bestSubarrayInfo;\n    traceResult.executionSummary = this.buildExecutionSummary(traceResult);\n    return traceResult;\n  }\n\n  computeBestSubarray(traceResult) {\n    const steps = traceResult.steps || [];\n    if (!steps.length) return null;\n\n    // Extract input array `nums` from the first step that has it\n    let numsArr = null;\n    for (const s of steps) {\n      const numsRow = (s.variables || []).find((v) => v.name === \"nums\" && Array.isArray(v.rawValue));\n      if (numsRow) {\n        numsArr = numsRow.rawValue;\n        break;\n      }\n    }\n    if (!numsArr || !numsArr.length) return null;\n\n    let bestSum = numsArr[0];\n    let bestStart = 0;\n    let bestEnd = 0;\n    let currentSum = 0;\n    let currentStart = 0;\n\n    for (let i = 0; i < numsArr.length; i++) {\n      if (currentSum === 0) currentStart = i;\n      currentSum += numsArr[i];\n      if (currentSum >= bestSum) {\n        bestSum = currentSum;\n        bestStart = currentStart;\n        bestEnd = i;\n      }\n      if (currentSum < 0) {\n        currentSum = 0;\n      }\n    }\n\n    return {\n      subarray: numsArr.slice(bestStart, bestEnd + 1),\n      startIndex: bestStart,\n      endIndex: bestEnd,\n      maxSum: bestSum\n    };\n  }\n\n  buildTeacherLesson(step, prevStep, nextStep, bestSubarrayInfo) {\n    const n = step.stepIndex;\n    const op = step.operationDetail || {};\n    const cond = step.condition;\n    const nextSentence = this.buildFriendlyWhatNext(step, nextStep);\n    const relevantVarsNow = this.formatRelevantVariablesNow(step);\n\n    // 1. Class definition\n    if (step.eventType === \"CLASS_DEF\") {\n      return {\n        title: `Step ${n}: Create the Solution class`,\n        calculationCard: null,\n        whatItMeans:\n          `Python reads \\`class Solution:\\`, which is a wrapper container that holds our function. Creating the class does not calculate the answer yet—it just prepares the container.`,\n        variableValuesNow: relevantVarsNow,\n        whatHappensNext: nextSentence,\n        finalBanner: null\n      };\n    }\n\n    // 2. Method / Function definition\n    if (step.eventType === \"METHOD_DEF\" || step.eventType === \"FUNC_DEF\") {\n      return {\n        title: `Step ${n}: Define the ${op.funcName} function`,\n        calculationCard: null,\n        whatItMeans:\n          `Python registers the function \\`${op.funcName}\\`, which takes a list of numbers called \\`${(op.params || [\"nums\"]).join(\", \")}\\`. Python only runs the code inside a function when we call it.`,\n        variableValuesNow: relevantVarsNow,\n        whatHappensNext: nextSentence,\n        finalBanner: null\n      };\n    }\n\n    // 3. Function Call\n    if (step.eventType === \"FUNC_CALL\") {\n      const b = (op.paramBindings || [])[0];\n      return {\n        title: `Step ${n}: Call the function with our list`,\n        calculationCard: null,\n        whatItMeans: b\n          ? `Now we call \\`${op.funcName}(nums)\\` and pass in our list \\`${b.val}\\`. Python jumps inside the function to start working through the steps!`\n          : `Now we call \\`${op.funcName}()\\` and jump inside the function to begin executing its lines.`,\n        variableValuesNow: relevantVarsNow,\n        whatHappensNext: nextSentence,\n        finalBanner: null\n      };\n    }\n\n    // 4. Standard variable assignment (`c = 0`, `ans = nums[0]`, `ans = c`, `c = 0`)\n    if (step.eventType === \"ASSIGN\") {\n      if (op.target === \"c\" && op.isCreated) {\n        return {\n          title: `Step ${n}: Create the variable c`,\n          calculationCard: null,\n          whatItMeans:\n            `We create a variable named \\`c\\` and store the number \\`${op.afterVal}\\` inside it. \\`c\\` will keep track of our running sum as we add numbers from the list.`,\n          variableValuesNow: relevantVarsNow,\n          whatHappensNext: nextSentence,\n          finalBanner: null\n        };\n      }\n      if (op.target === \"ans\" && op.isCreated) {\n        return {\n          title: `Step ${n}: Create the variable ans`,\n          calculationCard: null,\n          whatItMeans:\n            `We create a variable named \\`ans\\` and set it to the very first number in the list (\\`nums[0]\\`, which is \\`${op.afterVal}\\`). \\`ans\\` remembers the largest sum we have seen so far. Starting with \\`nums[0]\\` makes sure our code works even if every number in the list is negative!`,\n          variableValuesNow: relevantVarsNow,\n          whatHappensNext: nextSentence,\n          finalBanner: null\n        };\n      }\n      if (op.target === \"ans\" && !op.isCreated) {\n        return {\n          title: `Step ${n}: Save the new largest sum in ans`,\n          calculationCard: {\n            currentNumber: null,\n            before: `ans = ${op.beforeVal}`,\n            calculation: `ans = c (${op.afterVal})`,\n            after: `ans = ${op.afterVal}`\n          },\n          whatItMeans:\n            `Because our current sum \\`c\\` (\\`${op.afterVal}\\`) is at least as big as \\`ans\\` (\\`${op.beforeVal}\\`), we update \\`ans\\` to \\`${op.afterVal}\\`! This is our new best sum so far.`,\n          variableValuesNow: relevantVarsNow,\n          whatHappensNext: nextSentence,\n          finalBanner: null\n        };\n      }\n      if (op.target === \"c\" && op.afterVal === \"0\" && !op.isCreated) {\n        return {\n          title: `Step ${n}: Reset c to zero`,\n          calculationCard: {\n            currentNumber: null,\n            before: `c = ${op.beforeVal}`,\n            calculation: `Reset negative sum to 0`,\n            after: `c = 0`\n          },\n          whatItMeans:\n            `Because \\`c\\` was negative (\\`${op.beforeVal}\\`), keeping it would only make future sums smaller. So we reset \\`c\\` back to \\`0\\` to start a fresh continuous section on the next number!`,\n          variableValuesNow: relevantVarsNow,\n          whatHappensNext: nextSentence,\n          finalBanner: null\n        };\n      }\n\n      return {\n        title: `Step ${n}: ${op.isCreated ? \"Create\" : \"Update\"} the variable ${op.target}`,\n        calculationCard: op.isCreated\n          ? null\n          : {\n              currentNumber: null,\n              before: `${op.target} = ${op.beforeVal}`,\n              calculation: `${op.target} = ${op.substituted}`,\n              after: `${op.target} = ${op.afterVal}`\n            },\n        whatItMeans: op.isCreated\n          ? `We create a variable named \\`${op.target}\\` and store \\`${op.afterVal}\\` inside it.`\n          : `We calculate \\`${op.substituted}\\` and update \\`${op.target}\\` from \\`${op.beforeVal}\\` to \\`${op.afterVal}\\`.`,\n        variableValuesNow: relevantVarsNow,\n        whatHappensNext: nextSentence,\n        finalBanner: null\n      };\n    }\n\n    // 5. Addition / Augmented Assignment (`c += nums[i]`)\n    if (step.eventType === \"AUG_ASSIGN\") {\n      const afterNum = Number(op.afterVal);\n      const ansRow = (step.variables || []).find((v) => v.name === \"ans\");\n      const ansNum = ansRow ? Number(ansRow.current) : null;\n\n      let teacherNote = `We added \\`${op.rhsVal}\\` to \\`${op.target}\\`, changing \\`${op.target}\\` from \\`${op.beforeVal}\\` to \\`${op.afterVal}\\`.`;\n      if (op.target === \"c\") {\n        if (afterNum < 0 && ansNum !== null && afterNum >= ansNum) {\n          teacherNote = `We added \\`${op.rhsVal}\\` to \\`c\\`, giving \\`${op.afterVal}\\`. That matches or beats \\`ans\\` (\\`${ansNum}\\`), and because \\`c\\` is negative, the second condition will reset \\`c\\` to zero.`;\n        } else if (afterNum < 0) {\n          teacherNote = `We added \\`${op.rhsVal}\\` to \\`c\\`, giving \\`${op.afterVal}\\`. Because the result is negative, the \\`if c < 0:\\` check will reset \\`c\\` to zero.`;\n        } else if (ansNum !== null && afterNum >= ansNum) {\n          teacherNote = `We added \\`${op.rhsVal}\\` to \\`c\\`, bringing \\`c\\` up to \\`${op.afterVal}\\`! Because \\`${op.afterVal}\\` is at least as large as our best sum \\`ans\\` (\\`${ansNum}\\`), the next condition will update \\`ans\\` to \\`${op.afterVal}\\`!`;\n        } else {\n          teacherNote = `We added \\`${op.rhsVal}\\` to \\`c\\`, changing \\`c\\` from \\`${op.beforeVal}\\` to \\`${op.afterVal}\\`. Since \\`c\\` is still positive, we keep building this continuous section.`;\n        }\n      }\n\n      return {\n        title: `Step ${n}: Add the current number`,\n        calculationCard: {\n          currentNumber: op.rhsVal,\n          before: `${op.target} = ${op.beforeVal}`,\n          calculation: `${op.target} = ${op.beforeVal} ${op.baseOp} (${op.rhsVal})`,\n          after: `${op.target} = ${op.afterVal}`\n        },\n        whatItMeans: teacherNote,\n        variableValuesNow: relevantVarsNow,\n        whatHappensNext: nextSentence,\n        finalBanner: null\n      };\n    }\n\n    // 6. Loop iteration (`for i in range(len(nums)):`)\n    if (step.eventType === \"LOOP_ITER\" && op.kind === \"for_iter\") {\n      const elemInfo = op.indexedElementInfo;\n      return {\n        title: `Step ${n}: Loop pass ${op.iteration} of ${op.total} (i = ${op.iterVal})`,\n        calculationCard: elemInfo\n          ? {\n              currentNumber: elemInfo.elementVal,\n              before: `Position i = ${elemInfo.indexVal}`,\n              calculation: `Look up ${elemInfo.arrayName}[${elemInfo.indexVal}]`,\n              after: `Current number is ${elemInfo.elementVal}`\n            }\n          : null,\n        whatItMeans: elemInfo\n          ? `The loop moves to position \\`i = ${op.iterVal}\\` (item ${op.iteration} of ${op.total}). The number at \\`nums[${op.iterVal}]\\` is **\\`${elemInfo.elementVal}\\`**.`\n          : `The loop starts pass ${op.iteration} of ${op.total} and sets \\`${op.iterVar} = ${op.iterVal}\\`.`,\n        variableValuesNow: relevantVarsNow,\n        whatHappensNext: nextSentence,\n        finalBanner: null\n      };\n    }\n\n    // 7. Loop End\n    if (step.eventType === \"LOOP_END\") {\n      return {\n        title: `Step ${n}: Loop finished all numbers`,\n        calculationCard: null,\n        whatItMeans:\n          `We have checked every single number in the list! The loop is now finished, so Python leaves the loop and moves to the final \\`return\\` line.`,\n        variableValuesNow: relevantVarsNow,\n        whatHappensNext: nextSentence,\n        finalBanner: null\n      };\n    }\n\n    // 8. Condition Check (`if c >= ans:` or `if c < 0:`)\n    if (step.eventType === \"CONDITION\" && cond) {\n      let stepTitle = `Step ${n}: Check the condition (${cond.expr})`;\n      let explanation = \"\";\n\n      if (cond.expr === \"c >= ans\") {\n        stepTitle = `Step ${n}: Check if c (${cond.leftVal}) beats or ties ans (${cond.rightVal})`;\n        explanation = cond.result\n          ? `We ask: Is \\`c >= ans\\` (\\`Is ${cond.leftVal} >= ${cond.rightVal}\\`)? **Yes, True!** Our current sum \\`c\\` is at least as big as \\`ans\\`, so Python goes inside the \\`if\\` block to update \\`ans\\`.`\n          : `We ask: Is \\`c >= ans\\` (\\`Is ${cond.leftVal} >= ${cond.rightVal}\\`)? **No, False.** \\`${cond.leftVal}\\` is smaller than \\`${cond.rightVal}\\`, so \\`ans\\` stays \\`${cond.rightVal}\\` and Python skips this \\`if\\` block.`;\n      } else if (cond.expr === \"c < 0\") {\n        stepTitle = `Step ${n}: Check if c (${cond.leftVal}) is negative`;\n        explanation = cond.result\n          ? `We ask: Is \\`c < 0\\` (\\`Is ${cond.leftVal} < 0\\`)? **Yes, True!** Because \\`c\\` is negative (\\`${cond.leftVal}\\`), Python goes inside this \\`if\\` block to reset \\`c\\` back to \\`0\\`.`\n          : `We ask: Is \\`c < 0\\` (\\`Is ${cond.leftVal} < 0\\`)? **No, False.** Since \\`${cond.leftVal}\\` is not negative, we do not reset \\`c\\`—we keep this sum for the next number!`;\n      } else {\n        explanation = `We test \\`${cond.expr}\\` by comparing \\`${cond.leftVal} ${cond.operator} ${cond.rightVal}\\`, which is **${cond.result ? \"True\" : \"False\"}**.`;\n      }\n\n      return {\n        title: stepTitle,\n        calculationCard: {\n          currentNumber: null,\n          before: `${cond.leftExpr} is ${cond.leftVal}, ${cond.rightExpr} is ${cond.rightVal}`,\n          calculation: `${cond.leftVal} ${cond.operator} ${cond.rightVal}`,\n          after: cond.result ? \"True (Run the indented line)\" : \"False (Skip the indented line)\"\n        },\n        whatItMeans: explanation,\n        variableValuesNow: relevantVarsNow,\n        whatHappensNext: nextSentence,\n        finalBanner: null\n      };\n    }\n\n    // 9. Return Statement\n    if (step.eventType === \"RETURN\") {\n      const subText =\n        bestSubarrayInfo && bestSubarrayInfo.subarray\n          ? `The continuous section \\`[${bestSubarrayInfo.subarray.join(\", \")}]\\` has the largest sum: **${op.returnVal}**.`\n          : `The function finishes and returns the final answer: **${op.returnVal}**.`;\n\n      return {\n        title: `Step ${n}: Return the final answer (${op.returnVal})`,\n        calculationCard: null,\n        whatItMeans:\n          `We have finished checking the entire list! \\`return ans\\` sends our final largest sum **\\`${op.returnVal}\\`** back as the answer.`,\n        variableValuesNow: relevantVarsNow,\n        whatHappensNext: `The program is complete! You can click Restart or try a different list of numbers above.`,\n        finalBanner: {\n          answer: op.returnVal,\n          summary: subText\n        }\n      };\n    }\n\n    // Fallback for print / break / continue / exceptions\n    return {\n      title: `Step ${n}: Execute line ${step.line}`,\n      calculationCard: null,\n      whatItMeans:\n        step.eventType === \"PRINT\"\n          ? `Python displays \\`\"${op.output}\"\\` as output.`\n          : step.eventType === \"EXCEPTION\"\n          ? `Python stopped with an error: \\`${op.message}\\`.`\n          : `Python runs \\`${step.codeText}\\`.`,\n      variableValuesNow: relevantVarsNow,\n      whatHappensNext: nextSentence,\n      finalBanner: null\n    };\n  }\n\n  formatRelevantVariablesNow(step) {\n    const vars = step.variables || [];\n    // Filter out large `nums` list from the inline text summary so it focuses on `c`, `ans`, `i`, etc.\n    const compact = vars.filter((v) => v.name !== \"nums\");\n    if (compact.length === 0) {\n      if (vars.length > 0) {\n        return vars.map((v) => `${v.name} = ${v.current}`).join(\", \");\n      }\n      return \"No variables created yet\";\n    }\n    const parts = compact.map((v) => `${v.name} = ${v.current}`);\n    if (step.loop && step.loop.indexedElementInfo) {\n      const el = step.loop.indexedElementInfo;\n      parts.push(`${el.arrayName}[${el.indexVal}] = ${el.elementVal}`);\n    }\n    return parts.join(\"   •   \");\n  }\n\n  buildFriendlyWhatNext(step, nextStep) {\n    if (!nextStep) {\n      return \"We have reached the end of the program!\";\n    }\n    const nextCode = nextStep.codeText || \"\";\n    if (nextStep.eventType === \"METHOD_DEF\" || nextStep.eventType === \"FUNC_DEF\") {\n      return `Python moves to Line ${nextStep.line} to register the function \\`${nextStep.operationDetail.funcName}\\`.`;\n    }\n    if (nextStep.eventType === \"FUNC_CALL\") {\n      return `Python calls the function with our input list and enters the function body.`;\n    }\n    if (nextCode === \"c = 0\" && step.eventType === \"FUNC_CALL\") {\n      return `Python moves inside the function to Line ${nextStep.line} and creates the variable \\`c = 0\\`.`;\n    }\n    if (nextCode.startsWith(\"ans =\")) {\n      return nextCode === \"ans = nums[0]\"\n        ? `Python moves to Line ${nextStep.line} and creates the variable \\`ans\\` using the first number in the list.`\n        : `Because \\`c >= ans\\` was True, Python moves into the \\`if\\` block on Line ${nextStep.line} to update \\`ans = c\\`.`;\n    }\n    if (nextStep.eventType === \"LOOP_ITER\") {\n      const nextOp = nextStep.operationDetail || {};\n      return nextOp.iteration === 1\n        ? `Python moves to Line ${nextStep.line} to start the loop with the first number in the list (\\`i = 0\\`).`\n        : `Python loops back up to Line ${nextStep.line} to pick the next number in the list (\\`i = ${nextOp.iterVal}\\`).`;\n    }\n    if (nextStep.eventType === \"LOOP_END\") {\n      return `Python checks the loop header on Line ${nextStep.line}, sees there are no numbers left, and finishes the loop.`;\n    }\n    if (nextCode.startsWith(\"c +=\")) {\n      return `Python moves into the loop body on Line ${nextStep.line} and adds the current number \\`nums[i]\\` to \\`c\\`.`;\n    }\n    if (nextCode.startsWith(\"if c >= ans\")) {\n      return `Python moves to Line ${nextStep.line} to check if our new sum \\`c\\` is bigger than or equal to \\`ans\\`.`;\n    }\n    if (nextCode.startsWith(\"if c < 0\")) {\n      return `Python moves to Line ${nextStep.line} to check if \\`c\\` became a negative number.`;\n    }\n    if (nextCode === \"c = 0\") {\n      return `Because \\`c < 0\\` was True, Python moves to Line ${nextStep.line} and resets \\`c\\` back to \\`0\\`.`;\n    }\n    if (nextStep.eventType === \"RETURN\") {\n      return `The loop is done, so Python moves to Line ${nextStep.line} (\\`return ans\\`) to give back the final answer!`;\n    }\n    return `Python moves to Line ${nextStep.line} and runs \\`${nextCode}\\`.`;\n  }\n\n  // Keep technical & 7-part explanation builder for the optional Advanced View\n  buildStepExplanation(step, prevStep, nextStep) {\n    const lesson = step.teacherLesson || this.buildTeacherLesson(step, prevStep, nextStep, null);\n    const code = step.codeText || \"\";\n    const cond = step.condition;\n    const beforeVars = step.beforeVars || {};\n\n    const beforeKeys = Object.keys(beforeVars);\n    const variablesBefore =\n      beforeKeys.length === 0\n        ? \"No local variables existed before this step.\"\n        : beforeKeys.map((k) => `\\`${k} = ${beforeVars[k]}\\``).join(\", \");\n\n    let whyCondition = \"Not a condition line.\";\n    if (cond) {\n      whyCondition = `\\`${cond.leftVal} ${cond.operator} ${cond.rightVal}\\` evaluated to **${cond.result ? \"True\" : \"False\"}**.`;\n    }\n\n    return {\n      whatBeginner: lesson.whatItMeans,\n      whatTechnical: `Event \\`${step.eventType}\\` at Line ${step.line} in \\`${step.functionName}\\`: ${step.changedSummary}.`,\n      symbolsMeaning: this.explainSymbolsInLine(code),\n      whyExecuting: prevStep\n        ? `Moved from Line ${prevStep.line} to Line ${step.line}.`\n        : `First statement in the program.`,\n      variablesBefore,\n      whatChangesAfter: step.changedSummary || \"No variable changes.\",\n      whyCondition,\n      whatNext: lesson.whatHappensNext\n    };\n  }\n\n  explainSymbolsInLine(codeText) {\n    const matches = [];\n    for (const item of PYTHON_SYMBOLS_LIBRARY) {\n      if (codeText.includes(item.token)) {\n        matches.push(`• \\`${item.label}\\`: ${item.desc}`);\n      }\n    }\n    return matches.length ? matches.slice(0, 3).join(\"<br>\") : \"• Standard Python statement.\";\n  }\n\n  buildPracticeChallenge(step, nextStep) {\n    if (!nextStep) return null;\n    if (nextStep.eventType === \"CONDITION\" && nextStep.condition) {\n      const c = nextStep.condition;\n      return {\n        prompt: `Quick Check: On the next line (\\`${nextStep.codeText}\\`), will \\`${c.expr}\\` be True or False?`,\n        options: [\n          { label: `True (${c.leftVal} ${c.operator} ${c.rightVal})`, correct: c.result === true },\n          { label: `False (${c.leftVal} ${c.operator} ${c.rightVal})`, correct: c.result === false }\n        ],\n        explanation: `With \\`${c.leftExpr} = ${c.leftVal}\\` and \\`${c.rightExpr} = ${c.rightVal}\\`, the answer is **${c.result ? \"True\" : \"False\"}**.`\n      };\n    }\n    return null;\n  }\n\n  buildExecutionSummary(traceResult) {\n    if (!traceResult.ok || !traceResult.steps.length) {\n      return `Stopped: ${traceResult.errorMessage || \"Check syntax or input.\"}`;\n    }\n    if (traceResult.finalResult !== null) {\n      return `Final Answer: **${traceResult.finalResult}** (${traceResult.steps.length} steps)`;\n    }\n    return `Completed in ${traceResult.steps.length} steps.`;\n  }\n\n  answerBuiltInQuestion(questionId, step, traceResult) {\n    if (!step) return \"Click Next Step to start exploring.\";\n    const lesson = step.teacherLesson;\n    switch (questionId) {\n      case \"what_line_does\":\n        return lesson.whatItMeans;\n      case \"why_var_changed\":\n        return step.changedSummary;\n      case \"what_happens_next\":\n        return lesson.whatHappensNext;\n      case \"what_symbol_means\":\n        return step.explanations.symbolsMeaning;\n      default:\n        return lesson.whatItMeans;\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nwindow.RuleBasedExplainer = RuleBasedExplainer;\n","Description":"Update explainer.js to generate conversational \"Teach Me This Code\" lessons, calculation breakdowns, and final contiguous subarray explanations","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\CVT\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\code-flow-visualizer\\explainer.js","toolAction":"Updating explainer.js with Teach Me This Code lessons","toolSummary":"Update explainer.js for simple Teach Me This Code step format"}}]}
