 - On the final step, displays:\n       - **`Final answer: 6`**\n       - *\"The continuous section `[4, -1, 2, 1]` has the largest sum: 6.\"*\n   - **Area 3 — Variable Values (Right)**:\n     - Clean 2-column table (`Variable | Current value`) showing only relevant variables (`c`, `ans`, `i`, `nums[i]`), highlighting a row **only when its value changes**, plus a clean view of the input list `nums`.\n2. **Simple Navigation Controls**:\n   - Only **`← Previous`**, a prominent blue **`Next Step →`** button, **`▶ Auto Play`**, **`↺ Restart`**, and **`Step X of 50`**.\n3. **Optional \"Advanced View\" & \"Change Input / Code\" Buttons**:\n   - Technical debugging details (data types, scope metadata, symbol dictionary, and flowchart) are now hidden behind the optional **`Advanced View`** button in the top-right corner.\n\nRefresh **http://127.0.0.1:8080** in your browser (or press `Ctrl + F5`) to see the new **\"Teach Me This Code\"** interface!","thinking":"Examining the current modifications, the existing execution engine was preserved. The focus remained on ensuring its continued functionality with the recent changes.\n\n\nFocus shifted to the UI redesign, implementing the \"Teach Me This Code\" interface. Initial design included a \"Your Code\" section with line highlighting and a central teaching area for step-by-step explanations. Light theme and clean aesthetic were prioritized.\n\n\n"}
